questions.explanation:
This question tests end-to-end thinking for a real-time AWS ML workflow with PrivateLink, including model choice, training strategy, endpoint sizing, canary rollout, and monitoring for drift and privacy. Key concepts covered include SageMaker training with transfer learning on image-caption data, PrivateLink access to a VPC-hosted endpoint, real-time endpoint autoscaling and latency targeting, canary rollout and rollback criteria, and Model Monitor for drift and privacy checks.

```javascript
// Training config
const config = {
  encoder: 'EfficientNet-Lite0',
  decoder: 'TransformerDecoder',
  vocabularySize: 8000,
  augmentation: ['random_crop', 'horizontal_flip', 'color_jitter'],
  learningRate: 0.001,
  batchSize: 32,
  epochs: 20
};

// Endpoint config
const endpointConfig = {
  instanceType: 'ml.g4dn.xlarge',
  minInstances: 1,
  maxInstances: 3,
  scalingTarget: { metric: 'P99Latency', value: 500 },
  cooldown: 300
};

// Canary rollout
const canaryConfig = {
  initialTraffic: 5,
  stages: [5, 25, 50, 100],
  stageDuration: 86400,
  rollback: { latencyThreshold: 600, errorRateThreshold: 0.01 }
};
```

## Why This Is Asked
This evaluates expertise in deploying real-time ML systems within AWS for privacy-sensitive, multi-tenant environments requiring comprehensive monitoring, explainability, and rapid recovery capabilities.

## Key Concepts
- AWS PrivateLink and SageMaker endpoint architecture
- Private data lake integration with strict multi-tenant isolation
- Real-time drift detection and SHAP/IG explainability frameworks
- Provisioned concurrency and autoscaling for performance targets

## Code Example
```javascript
// Explainer integration for inference transparency
function explainInference(model, input, featureNames) {
  const shapValues = model.predictSHAP(input);
  const igValues = model.predictIntegratedGradients(input);
  return {
    prediction: model.predict(input),
    explanations: {
      shap: shapValues,
      integratedGradients: igValues,
      featureNames: featureNames
    },
    timestamp: new Date().toISOString(),
    tenantId: extractTenantId(input)
  };
}
```
